Done. Here's what I implemented:

**`parse_git_status_counts(porcelain: &str) -> (u32, u32, u32)** — a pure function that parses git status --porcelain` output into (staged, modified, untracked) counts. Each porcelain line has two status columns: index (column 0) and worktree (column 1). Lines starting with ?? are untracked; other non-space index chars mean staged; other non-space worktree chars mean modified.

**git_status_summary() -> Option<String>** — calls run_git(["status", "--porcelain"]), returns "clean" for empty output, or a comma-separated summary like "3 staged, 2 modified, 1 untracked".

`print_banner()` — now appends  · <status> after the project context line, so the banner reads:
```
  📁 Rust project (yoyo-evolve) on main · 2 modified, 1 staged
```

